[0.009803, "o", "\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\ncorro 0.7.0 on the zork backend\r\n"]
[0.013088, "o", "------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n\r\n[part 1 of 3]  The app builds its GUI tree, then records what it built\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nThe widget tree is corro's real GUI construction path, built against the\r\nin-memory model instead of a display. The record is written to a file,\r\nbecause it has to be taken while the tree is still live: the REPL adopts\r\nthe model on startup, after which all 98 nodes are gone.\r\n\r\n  $ echo quit | CORRO_ZORK_WALKTHROUGH=<file> ./target/debug/corro\r\n\r\n"]
[0.029645, "o", "corro 0.7.0 on the zork backend\r\n======================================================\r\n\r\nThe widget tree above this text is corro's real GUI tree,\r\nbuilt against an in-memory model instead of a display.\r\n\r\n"]
